  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 210 AM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nThe upper-level low across the southwest U.S. will eventually \nlift into the Southern Plains by Monday. Moisture is somewhat \nlimited, but there is currently a ~10% chance of rain on Monday \nassociated with this system. \n\nBeyond Monday, warm afternoons and cool nights will continue with\nhighs generally in the 60s and 70s and lows generally in the 40s \nand 50s deg F. A cold front may pass by late Thursday into \nFriday, but no significant cool down is expected in its wake. Even\nthe cooler end of bias-corrected probabilistic guidance (i.e., \nthe 10th percentile) has high temperatures only dropping into the \n50s deg F, which is only slightly below normal for mid-November. \n\nMahale",
